  "details": "- CVE-2026-82720: pop each reply off the mesh reply list before it is\n  dropped or answered, detach the tcp_req_info and DoH stream references\n  and clear the h2 stream mesh states when a DoH session is dropped, so\n  an RPZ drop or jostled query can no longer leave a dangling DoH stream\n  reference that is used after free\n- CVE-2026-77955: do not serve or write to disk a zonemd-check zone\n  while its ZONEMD verification is still pending; the zonefile write is\n  deferred to the ZONEMD callback and done only if the zone verified\n- CVE-2026-85501: bound the DNSSEC work per validation (ReTrap): add the\n  val-validation-attempts and val-hash-attempts limits (default 32),\n  limit DNSKEY/RRSIG and DS key-tag matches and NSEC/NSEC3 records\n  checked, shorten oversized referral DS RRsets, stop validator restarts\n  once the limits are hit, and require only the answer and authority\n  sections to be secure; the built-in val-clean-additional default is\n  now no, the shipped unbound.conf keeps val-clean-additional: yes",
